WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.735
When does the Lok Sabha seat

2
00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.319
freeze end?

3
00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:03.906
In 2026?

4
00:00:04.406 --> 00:00:05.430
Not quite.

5
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.316
The Constitution ties it

6
00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:08.852
to a census, not a date.

7
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:11.276
Article 82 says seats need

8
00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:12.566
not be readjusted

9
00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:14.688
until figures from the first

10
00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:16.637
census taken after 2026 are

11
00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:17.359
published.

12
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:20.203
Until then, seats among states

13
00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:22.119
rest on the 1971 census.

14
00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:24.858
The 84th Amendment, in 2001,

15
00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.003
set that rule.

16
00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:29.393
The 87th, in 2003, let boundaries

17
00:00:29.393 --> 00:00:32.248
be redrawn on the 2001 census.

18
00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:35.027
The next census counts people

19
00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:38.159
as of 1 March 2027, its reference date.

20
00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:40.517
In April 2026, a bill to

21
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.823
remove that link

22
00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:43.461
failed to get the two-thirds

23
00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:44.505
majority it needed.

24
00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:46.529
So the clock is a census,

25
00:00:46.529 --> 00:00:47.600
not the calendar.

26
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.975
Your turn.

27
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:50.480
Which census will end the

28
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.130
seat freeze?
